From 33582bc1967b5a8d4249e52b5772a95090ac5a3b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Mohamed R. Khalil" <m.radwan.khalil@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 21:04:59 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] fix(hooks): patch tool args on the object opencode executes;
 follow the configured shell

opencode triggers tool.execute.before with `{ args }` and then runs the tool
with its own `args` reference. It never reads `output.args` back. replaceToolArgs
replaced `output.args` with a clone, so every argument rewrite was dropped: the
git non-interactive environment, Claude hook updatedInput, the NUL-byte strip,
and the todos/prompt/subagent_type/questions/url rewrites. It also detached the
object for every plugin hook that runs after this plugin, whose in-place edits
were lost too.

replaceToolArgs now edits the object in place and falls back to replacing it
only when the object is frozen (the case the helper was written for).

With the rewrite live, the env prefix has to be in the syntax of the shell that
runs the command. The server environment cannot tell: Git Bash on Windows is
`"shell": "bash"` in the opencode config with no SHELL set, and the hook chose
cmd or PowerShell syntax. The hook now reads `shell` from the opencode config
(once, cached on success) and falls back to environment detection.
